@startuml
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #0b7a75
skinparam ComponentBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #6b7280
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #f3f4f6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9ca3af

skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam SequenceLifeLineBorderColor #9ca3af

title One FindCare search end to end, target architecture: the gate is a dumb facade,\nthe UniversalNavigator drives the map, tools call tools, Geo resolves geography in parallel\nwith the specialty filter, and the UtteranceManager authors the user-facing prose

participant "Gate\n(facade, transport only)" as Gate
participant "UniversalNavigator\n(SharedServices main)" as UN
participant "UtteranceManager\n(classify + prose capability)" as UM
database "Registry\n(the one live map)" as Reg
database "Repository\nsessions, ledger, params" as Repo
participant "facility_search\n(tool)" as FS
participant "Miner\nmine_facility_parameters" as Miner
participant "SpecialtyFilter\nNon-Individual" as Cat
participant "Geo\n(page-scoped tool)" as Geo
database "Provider\ncollection" as Providers

[-> Gate : POST /  { session_token, head,\nparams(utterance, history) }  client_sessioned
activate Gate
note over Gate
  The gate knows only transport. It collects the token, the HTTP
  head, and the POST/GET parameters, each if present, and hands
  them to the navigator. It has no routes of its own; one generic
  gate module serves every container.
end note

Gate -> UN : navigate(session_token, head, params)
activate UN
UN -> Reg : the live map for this env\n(routes, may_call, required inputs)
Reg --> UN : routes + dependencies
note left of UN
  The navigator holds no data. The map is the registry,
  parameters ride the passed document, the session and the
  render ledger are repository rows. It is the only node
  that accepts external traffic.
end note
UN -> Repo : verify session_token, advance nonce,\nload parameters in force
Repo --> UN : session ok, in-force parameters

UN -> UM : classify(utterance, history)
activate UM
UM --> UN : dispatch set { facility_search }
deactivate UM
note right of UM
  One model call: the cached preamble plus every tool's registry
  fragment in, routes out. It knows no parameters and never waits
  on a tool - it returns the set; parallelism is the point.
end note

UN -> Repo : record the render-ledger expectation
UN -> FS : dispatch { utterance, history, in-force params }
activate FS
FS -> Miner : mine(utterance, history)
activate Miner
Miner --> FS : geography(free text), facilityType, facilityName
deactivate Miner

par SpecialtyFilter resolves the kind of place
  alt a kind of place was named
    FS -> Cat : find_specialties(facilityType, Non-Individual)
    activate Cat
    Cat --> FS : offered kinds + codes
    deactivate Cat
  end
else Geo resolves geography, in parallel
  FS -> Geo : resolve(free-text geography)
  activate Geo
  Geo --> FS : normalized place (state, ZIP, county),\nmisspellings and city/county-without-state repaired
  deactivate Geo
end
note over FS, Geo
  Geo is a page-scoped member (individualProvider + facility), running
  parallel to the specialty/NUCC filter. It resolves free-text geography
  including misspellings and a city or county named without a state -
  it replaces the old ad-hoc "derive the state from the ZIP" step.
  Tools call tools directly along the non-circular may_call map, with
  recursion guards. A tool in the middle re-raises and never swallows;
  every throw ends in a navigator, which catches, classifies, logs with
  timings, and answers.
end note
FS --> UN : completion callback { mined document, UserRefinementRequestText }\ninternal_callback, proof our_signature
deactivate FS
UN -> Repo : close the ledger entry, then serial deterministic\nmerge into parameter state (a conflict is an exception)
UN -> UN : completeness test - the passed document\nagainst the registry's required inputs

alt required inputs all in force
  UN -> FS : dispatch { search: codes, place }
  activate FS
  FS -> Providers : search_providers(entity_type = "2", codes, place)
  Providers --> FS : rows + total
  FS --> UN : completion callback { rows, UserRefinementRequestText }\ninternal_callback, proof our_signature
  deactivate FS
  UN -> Repo : close the ledger entry, serial merge the rows
else a required input is unmet
  UN -> UM : prose: RequestUsersRefinement()\n{ unmet, in force, utterance }
  activate UM
  UM --> UN : the user-facing sentence
  deactivate UM
  note right of UM
    RequestUsersRefinement is a capability of the UtteranceManager, not a
    separate tool - one conversational surface; no tool talks to the user
    directly. It has two forms, both inside the UM:
    RequestUsersRefinement() - when classification finds no dispatchable
    route or a missing slot, the UM's own LLM authors the question (shown
    above); RequestUsersRefinement(question) - a dispatched tool authored
    the question, carried on the tool's UserRefinementRequestText field
    (empty = the tool is answering), and the UM only delivers it.
    Approved requirements place prose and parameters inside the UM
    (EPIC-002-F-010-S-001, EPIC-002-F-010-S-003, EPIC-006-F-008-S-003).
    Making a parameter required is a registry edit and a deploy, not code.
  end note
end

UN --> Gate : the merged answer, sequenced
deactivate UN
[<-- Gate : the one stream the gate writes
deactivate Gate

@enduml
